# ============================================================================
# Range A : F_00178 .. F_04950  (system layer: GodLib + Pure C runtime helpers)
# Names follow GodLib (a later version is in ref/GODLIB) in Module_Action style.
# GodLib modules without an allowed prefix were mapped as follows:
#   GRAPHIC -> Screen_Gfx*, SPRITE -> Screen_Sprite*, FADE -> Video_Fade*,
#   LINKFILE -> File_Link*, BASE sTagString -> Str_Tag*.
# ============================================================================

# ---- AUDIO MIXER (GodLib AUDIO/AMIXER.C) : 2 software voices mixed into the DMA ring buffer ----
F_00178 AudioMixer_Init
@AudioMixer_Init AudioMixer_Init() : GodLib AudioMixer_Init. Sets gAudioMixerDmaHw if the machine has DMA sound (STE/MegaSTE/TT/Falcon),
@AudioMixer_Init allocates the 4 KB silence buffer and the 10 KB mix ring buffer in ST-RAM, builds the 64 KB volume table
@AudioMixer_Init (entry [vol][sample] = signed sample * vol / 256) and points both voices at the silence buffer.
@AudioMixer_Init Voice layout (16 bytes): +0 pStart, +4 pCurrent, +8 length, +d volume (set to $ff, unused by the mixer), +e pan (0 = left .. 255 = right), +f active flag.
F_00252 AudioMixer_DeInit
@AudioMixer_DeInit AudioMixer_DeInit() : GodLib AudioMixer_DeInit. Stops the mixer, silences both voices, frees silence and mix buffers.
F_00294 AudioMixer_Enable
@AudioMixer_Enable AudioMixer_Enable() : GodLib AudioMixer_Enable. If DMA hardware is present: adds the mixer VBL routine (L_01cca),
@AudioMixer_Enable resets both voices, then starts a looping 8 KB, 8-bit stereo, 50 kHz DMA sound on the ring buffer.
F_00318 AudioMixer_Disable
@AudioMixer_Disable AudioMixer_Disable() : GodLib AudioMixer_Disable. If enabled: stops DMA playback ($ffff8901) and removes the mixer VBL routine.
F_00342 AudioMixer_PlaySample
@AudioMixer_PlaySample d0 = AudioMixer_PlaySample(a0 = sAudioDmaSound*, d0 = pan) : GodLib AudioMixer_PlaySample.
@AudioMixer_PlaySample Starts the sample on the first free voice. Returns 1 if a voice was free, 0 otherwise.
F_00388 AudioMixer_PlaySampleDirect
@AudioMixer_PlaySampleDirect d0 = AudioMixer_PlaySampleDirect(a0 = sAudioDmaSound*, d0 = pan) : GodLib AudioMixer_PlaySampleDirect.
@AudioMixer_PlaySampleDirect Uses a free voice, or steals the voice with the fewest bytes left to play. Always returns 1.
F_00402 AudioMixer_CanPlayNewSpl
@AudioMixer_CanPlayNewSpl d0 = AudioMixer_CanPlayNewSpl() : GodLib AudioMixer_CanPlayNewSpl. 1 if at least one voice is free.
F_01da4 AudioMixer_MixChunk
@AudioMixer_MixChunk AudioMixer_MixChunk(d0 = bytes, a0/a1 = voice 0/1 read pointers, a3/a5 = volume rows, a2 = destination) :
@AudioMixer_MixChunk inner mixing loop called by the mixer VBL routine (L_01cca). Adds the two voices through the volume
@AudioMixer_MixChunk table and writes each mixed byte pair 4 times (8 bytes per source byte) into the DMA ring buffer.
F_01e3c AudioMixer_AdvanceVoices
@AudioMixer_AdvanceVoices AudioMixer_AdvanceVoices(d0 = bytes mixed) : moves each active voice forward by d0/8 source bytes and
@AudioMixer_AdvanceVoices frees the voice (points it back at silence) once it has passed its end.
B_214e0 gAudioMixerVoices
B_1b9a2 gAudioMixerDmaHw
D_196ba gpAudioMixerBuffer
D_196be gpAudioMixerSilence
D_196c2 gpAudioMixerVolumeTable
D_196c6 gAudioMixerBufferOffset
D_196ca gAudioMixerLockFlag
D_196cb gAudioMixerEnableFlag

# ---- AUDIO (GodLib AUDIO/AUDIO.C, AUDIO_S.S) : YM2149, keyclick, DMA sound ----
F_00426 Audio_Init
@Audio_Init Audio_Init() : GodLib Audio_Init. Saves the YM registers, saves the DMA sound registers (STE or Falcon layout),
@Audio_Init remembers the keyclick and internal speaker states, then turns keyclick off, speaker on and silences the YM.
F_00496 Audio_DeInit
@Audio_DeInit Audio_DeInit() : GodLib Audio_DeInit. Restores keyclick, internal speaker, DMA sound registers and YM registers.
F_004e6 Audio_GetKeyClickState
@Audio_GetKeyClickState d0 = Audio_GetKeyClickState() : GodLib Audio_GetKeyClickState. Bit 0 of the system variable conterm ($484).
F_004f6 Audio_SetKeyClickState
@Audio_SetKeyClickState Audio_SetKeyClickState(d0 = on/off) : GodLib Audio_SetKeyClickState. Writes bit 0 of conterm ($484).
F_00508 Audio_GetSpeakerState
@Audio_GetSpeakerState d0 = Audio_GetSpeakerState() : GodLib Audio_GetInternalSpeakerState. Reads YM port A (register 14) bit 6.
F_0051e Audio_SetSpeakerState
@Audio_SetSpeakerState Audio_SetSpeakerState(d0 = state) : GodLib Audio_SetInternalSpeakerState. Writes YM port A (register 14) bit 6.
F_0053c Audio_DmaPlaySound
@Audio_DmaPlaySound Audio_DmaPlaySound(a0 = sAudioDmaSound*) : GodLib Audio_DmaPlaySound. Programs the STE/Falcon DMA sound
@Audio_DmaPlaySound start/end addresses and mode, then starts playback (looping if requested). Keeps a copy in gAudioCurrentDmaSound.
@Audio_DmaPlaySound sAudioDmaSound (12 bytes): +0 pSound, +4 length, +8 frequency (0..3), +9 bits (0 = 8 bit), +a loop flag, +b stereo flag.
F_01ec2 Audio_SaveYM
@Audio_SaveYM Audio_SaveYM() : GodLib Audio_SaveYM. Copies the 16 YM2149 registers into gAudioSavedRegs (with interrupts off).
F_01ee8 Audio_RestoreYM
@Audio_RestoreYM Audio_RestoreYM() : GodLib Audio_RestoreYM. Writes back the 16 YM2149 registers saved by Audio_SaveYM.
F_01f12 Audio_SaveDmaSte
@Audio_SaveDmaSte Audio_SaveDmaSte() : GodLib Audio_SaveDmaSte. Saves the STE DMA control and mode registers ($8901, $8921).
F_01f2e Audio_RestoreDmaSte
@Audio_RestoreDmaSte Audio_RestoreDmaSte() : GodLib Audio_RestoreDmaSte. Restores the STE DMA control and mode registers.
F_01f4a Audio_SaveDmaFalcon
@Audio_SaveDmaFalcon Audio_SaveDmaFalcon() : GodLib Audio_SaveDmaFalcon. Saves the Falcon DMA sound / crossbar / codec registers.
F_01f9e Audio_RestoreDmaFalcon
@Audio_RestoreDmaFalcon Audio_RestoreDmaFalcon() : GodLib Audio_RestoreDmaFalcon. Restores the Falcon registers saved by Audio_SaveDmaFalcon.
