# ---- FADE / SPRITE / GRAPHIC helpers (GodLib FADE, SPRITE, GRAPHIC) ----
F_00668 Video_FadePalSTE
@Video_FadePalSTE Video_FadePalSTE(a0 = dest pal, a1 = source pal, stack = target pal, d0 = colour count, d1 = pos 0..256) :
@Video_FadePalSTE GodLib Fade_PalSTE. For each colour, interpolates every 4-bit STE component from source to target
@Video_FadePalSTE (dest = src + (target - src) * pos / 256) using the STE<->linear conversion tables at VideoFadeSteToLinear.
D_1960c VideoFadeSteToLinear
F_00798 Screen_SpriteRelocate
@Screen_SpriteRelocate Screen_SpriteRelocate(a0 = sSprite*) : GodLib Sprite_Relocate. Turns the gfx (+0) and mask (+4) offsets into addresses.
F_007a2 Screen_SpriteBlockRelocate
@Screen_SpriteBlockRelocate Screen_SpriteBlockRelocate(a0 = sprite block) : GodLib Sprite_BlockRelocate. Block = {U32 id; U16 version;
@Screen_SpriteBlockRelocate U16 count; sSprite *sprites[count]}. Relocates the sprite pointer table, then every sprite. Used after loading .BSB files.
F_008d0 Screen_GfxInit
@Screen_GfxInit Screen_GfxInit() : GodLib Graphic_Init. Fills the 4-plane entries of the graphic function tables gScreenGfxFuncs
@Screen_GfxInit (normal and clipped, $24 bytes per colour mode) with the blitter routines if a blitter is present, else the CPU routines.
F_009b0 Screen_GfxDeInit
@Screen_GfxDeInit Screen_GfxDeInit() : GodLib Graphic_DeInit. Empty in this build.
F_009b2 Screen_CanvasInit
@Screen_CanvasInit Screen_CanvasInit(a0 = canvas, d0 = colour mode, d1 = width, d2 = height) : GodLib GraphicCanvas_Init.
@Screen_CanvasInit Stores mode/width/height (+4/+6/+8), builds the line offset table at +$14 (height capped to 1024)
@Screen_CanvasInit and points +$c / +$10 at the normal / clipped function tables for that colour mode.
B_1b9b4 gScreenGfxFuncs
F_01ff2 Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClip
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClip Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClip(a0 = canvas, a1 = dest pos, a2 = source rect, ...) : GodLib Graphic_4BP_Blit_Clip.
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClip 4-plane CPU blit with clipping; the block also contains the other CPU drawing routines
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClip (L_02072 blit, box, pixel, sprite...) whose addresses Screen_GfxInit stores. The entry itself is never called.
F_02c86 Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClipBlt
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClipBlt Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClipBlt(a0 = canvas, a1 = dest pos, a2 = source rect, ...) : GodLib Graphic_4BP_Blit_Clip_BLT.
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClipBlt Blitter version of the clipped blit; the block also holds the blitter drawing routines (L_02d06...)
@Screen_Gfx4BP_BlitClipBlt used by Screen_GfxInit on machines with a blitter. The entry itself is never called.

