# ---- LINK FILE (GodLib LINKFILE/LINKFILE.C) : packed archive read from disk on demand ----
F_00c5e File_LinkInit
@File_LinkInit a0 = File_LinkInit(a0 = archive name) : GodLib LinkFile_Init. Opens the archive, reads its 26-byte header, loads the
@File_LinkInit whole directory (FAT) into memory, relocates it and keeps the open file handle at +$14. Returns 0 on failure.
@File_LinkInit Folder: +0 file count, +2 folder count, +4 name, +8 files (20 bytes each: +0 packed size, +4 unpacked size, +8 offset, +$10 name), +c sub-folders (16 bytes each).
F_00cd8 File_LinkDeInit
@File_LinkDeInit File_LinkDeInit(a0 = link file) : GodLib LinkFile_DeInit. Closes the archive file and frees the directory.
F_00cf6 File_LinkFileLoad
@File_LinkFileLoad a0 = File_LinkFileLoad(a0 = link file, a1 = path, d0 = depack flag, d1 = ST-RAM flag) : GodLib LinkFile_FileLoad.
@File_LinkFileLoad Allocates a buffer (unpacked size if depacking; ST-RAM if d1), reads the file data from the archive and depacks it
@File_LinkFileLoad (Ice or Atomik) when asked. Returns the buffer, or 0.
F_00d74 File_LinkFileLoadAt
@File_LinkFileLoadAt d0 = File_LinkFileLoadAt(a0 = link file, a1 = path, stack = buffer, d0 = depack flag) : GodLib LinkFile_FileLoadAt.
@File_LinkFileLoadAt Same as File_LinkFileLoad but into a caller buffer. Returns 1 on success.
F_00dca File_LinkFileGetSize
@File_LinkFileGetSize d0 = File_LinkFileGetSize(a0 = link file, a1 = path, d0 = unpacked flag) : GodLib LinkFile_FileGetSize.
@File_LinkFileGetSize Returns the unpacked (d0 != 0) or packed size of a file in the archive, or 0 if not found.
F_00df8 File_LinkRelocateFolder
@File_LinkRelocateFolder File_LinkRelocateFolder(a0 = folder, d0 = base) : GodLib LinkFile_RelocateFolder. Adds base to the folder's
@File_LinkRelocateFolder pointers and to every file name pointer, recursing into the sub-folders.
F_00e4e File_LinkRelocate
@File_LinkRelocate File_LinkRelocate(a0 = link file) : GodLib LinkFile_Relocate. Relocates the root folder pointer (+$16) and the whole tree.
F_00e64 File_LinkGetpFolder
@File_LinkGetpFolder a0 = File_LinkGetpFolder(a0 = folder, a1 = name) : GodLib LinkFile_GetpFolder. Sub-folder with that name, or 0.
F_00ea8 File_LinkGetpFile
@File_LinkGetpFile a0 = File_LinkGetpFile(a0 = link file, a1 = path) : GodLib LinkFile_GetpFile. Walks the path ('/' or '\' separators,
@File_LinkGetpFile names upper-cased) through the folders and returns the file entry, or 0.

